# phaseest: 5-qubit quantum phase estimation circuit (NMR implementation)
# Constructed following Nielsen & Chuang [21] p.221 adapted for liquid-state NMR.
#
# Qubits:
#   q0 = target (eigenstate register)
#   q1, q2, q3, q4 = counting register (control qubits)
#
# Gate types:  1 = single-qubit (Ry/Rz),  2 = two-qubit (ZZ)
# T values:    T=1 for Ry(90) or ZZ(90),  T=0 for Rz (free gate)
#              T=2 for ZZ(180), T=4 for ZZ(360), T=0.5 for ZZ(45), etc.
#
# Structure:
#   Phase 1: H = Ry(90) on counting register   [levels 0]
#   Phase 2: Controlled-U^(2^k) on each qi     [levels 1-4]
#   Phase 3: Inverse QFT on counting register   [levels 5-11]
#   Free Rz: phase-frame corrections throughout [T=0]
#
# Two-qubit interactions present:
#   (q1,q0),(q2,q0),(q3,q0),(q4,q0)          [controlled-U gates]
#   (q3,q4),(q2,q4),(q2,q3)                   [IQFT stage 1]
#   (q1,q4),(q1,q3),(q1,q2)                   [IQFT stage 2]
#
# Interaction graph = K5 (complete on 5 nodes) -> needs rich physical environment
5
# --- Phase 1: Initialize counting register (H = Ry(90), T=1) ---
1 1 1.0 0
1 2 1.0 0
1 3 1.0 0
1 4 1.0 0
# --- Phase 2: Controlled-U^(2^k) gates ---
# CU on q1 (ZZ(90), T=1)
2 1 0 1.0 1
# CU^2 on q2 (ZZ(180), T=2)
2 2 0 2.0 2
# CU^4 on q3 (ZZ(360), T=4)
2 3 0 4.0 3
# CU^8 on q4 (ZZ(720), T=8)
2 4 0 8.0 4
# Rz frame corrections after controlled-U (T=0, free)
1 0 0.0 4
1 1 0.0 4
1 2 0.0 4
# --- Phase 3: Inverse QFT on q4, q3, q2, q1 ---
# Step 1: H on q4
1 4 1.0 5
# Step 2: controlled-R2 = ZZ(45) on (q3, q4)
2 3 4 0.5 6
# Step 3: H on q3
1 3 1.0 7
# Step 4: controlled-R2 and R3 on q2 (two ZZ gates, parallel)
2 2 4 0.25 8
2 2 3 0.5 8
# Step 5: H on q2
1 2 1.0 9
# Step 6: controlled-R2, R3, R4 on q1 (three ZZ gates, parallel)
2 1 4 0.125 10
2 1 3 0.25 10
2 1 2 0.5 10
# Step 7: H on q1
1 1 1.0 11
# Final Rz frame corrections (T=0, free)
1 0 0.0 12
1 1 0.0 12
1 2 0.0 12
1 3 0.0 12
1 4 0.0 12
